u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, DECEMBER 9, 2009\r\rMayor Wolfson called the meeting to order at 7:02 p.m. in the City Council Chambers, 100 Civic Center Way, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Wolfson, Mayor pro Tem Groveman, Councilmembers Bozajian, Maurer and Washburn.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Bartlett, Colantuono, Coroalles, Peirce, Tamuri, Yalda.\r \r The Pledge of Allegiance was led by Cadette Troop 1001. \r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r \rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian, to approve the agenda with the addition of Urgency Item, �Discussion of Letter to the Calabasas Chamber,� to the agenda with Councilmember Washburn�s RECUSAL on the Urgency Item. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS \r\rMayor Wolfson introduced Trent Adler, who sang �The Chaparral Spirit Song.� Mayor Wolfson presented proclamations to members of Cadette Troop 1001 and Junior Girl Scout Troop 68 in recognition of their community service work. Councilmember Bozajian spoke regarding the activities in honor of the 10th Anniversary of the Agoura Hills/Calabasas Community Center. Councilmember Maurer announced that the 2010 Community Recycling Program calendar is available at City Hall. \r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT \r\r No one indicated a desire to speak.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS \r\r Approval of meeting minutes from October 28, 2009. \r\rMayor pro Tem Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to approve Consent Item #1. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rPUBLIC HEARINGS \r\r Consideration and certification of a mitigated negative declaration, and introduction of Ordinance No. 2009-265 amending the City of Calabasas development code and zoning map to bring these documents into conformance with the policies and programs of the City of Calabasas 2030 General Plan, as recommended by the Planning Commission and pursuant to Calabasas Municipal Code Chapter 17.76.\r\r Mayor Wolfson opened the public hearing.\r\r Tom Bartlett, City Planner, presented the staff report.\r\r Kim Lamorie, Las Virgenes Homeowners Federation, spoke regarding the scenic corridor, including the public on lot line adjustments, and clustering in residential development zone. MaryEllen Strote, Cold Creek Community Council, spoke regarding fencing in the wildlife corridor. David Freedman, Agoura, spoke in support of the parallel slope measurement for height measurements in hillside development and spoke regarding swimming pools not being considered pervious surfaces. Nancy Rothenberg, Calabasas Highlands Homeowners Association, spoke regarding proposed changes to the development code regarding clustering, call for review and review authority. Helene Regan, Calabasas, spoke in opposition to making swimming pools a pervious surface. Emma Wilby, Calabasas, spoke regarding proposed language regarding maintenance work on and additions to non-conforming structures and height measuring requirements. Mary Hubbard, representing Save Open Space and Malibu Canyon Community Association, spoke regarding a letter from the Regional Water Quality Board regarding swimming pools being counted as pervious surfaces. Valerie Burkholder, Calabasas, spoke in opposition to clustering in residential zoning and retaining the City�s current requirements for hobby farms. Robert Pope, Calabasas Park Homeowners Association, spoke in opposition to swimming pools being counted as pervious surfaces.\r\r The City Council recessed at 9:04 p.m. and reconvened at 9:18 p.m.\r\r The City Council provided direction to staff regarding various components of the development code.\r\r Mayor Wolfson closed the public hearing.\r\r This item was CONTINUED to the January 13, 2010 regular City Council meeting.\r\rNEW BUSINESS \r\r Consideration of a request from Thomas Safran Associates, developer of the approved 75-unit senior affordable housing project at 4803 El Canon Avenue, to identify the City as a co-recipient for the $3,653,280.00 Infill Infrastructure Grant Award from the California Department of Housing and Community Development (HCD).� ��\r\rAndrew Gross, Thomas Safran & Associates, provided background information on the request to Council. Fred Gaines, Thomas Safran & Associates, spoke in support of the City acting as co-recipient for the Grant from the State of California.\r\r Mayor pro Tem Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to approve the request from Thomas Safran Associates, developer of the approved 75-unit senior affordable housing project at 4803 El Canon Avenue, to identify the City as a co-recipient for the $3,653,280.00 Infill Infrastructure Grant Award from the California Department of Housing and Community Development (HCD) by a roll call vote:\r\rAYES: Mayor Wolfson, Mayor pro Tem Groveman, and Councilmember Washburn.\rNOES: Councilmember Bozajian.\rABSTAIN: Councilmember Maurer.\r\r Review of a proposed ordinance amending the Calabasas Municipal Code to require encroachment permits for major construction projects within the Old Topanga Overlay Zone, the Calabasas Highlands Overlay Zone and the Park Moderne Overlay Zone.\r\rAndrew Brozyna, Deputy Public Works Director, presented the staff report.\r\rKim Lamorie, Calabasas, Las Virgenes Homeowners Federation, Nancy Rothenberg, Calabasas Highlands Homeowners Association, MaryEllen Strote, Cold Creek Community Council, spoke in support of and Emma Wilby, Calabasas, read a letter from Jody Thomas, Old Topanga Canyon Homeowners Association, in support of the proposed ordinance with the recommendation to limit the amount of construction projects to two at one time. Norm Dornfest, Calabasas, spoke in opposition to the proposed ordinance.\r\rThe City Council provided direction to staff regarding the proposed ordinance.\r\r Discussion regarding City support of a special project at Headwaters Corners.\r\rCouncilmember Maurer presented background information about the request.\r\r\r\rMayor pro Tem Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian to approve providing a $50,000 grant to Mountains Restoration Trust to�secure a team of consultants through the RFP process to prepare the Headwaters Corner Architectural Design Study for the development of facilities and site features at Headwaters Corners. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS \r\r Check Register for the period of October 19, 2009 to November 25, 2009. \r\rThere was no action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS \r\r Councilmember Maurer and Mayor Wolfson spoke regarding a recent City � School Partnership Meeting.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT \r\r City Manager Coroalles indicated that he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\r\r There were no future agenda items requested.\r\rThe City Council adjourned the regular meeting at 10:58 p.m. and reconvened into a special meeting.\r\r Councilmember Washburn recused himself and left the Council Chambers.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r \rMayor pro Tem Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Washburn was recused. \r\rURGENCY ITEM\r\rDiscussion of Letter to the Calabasas Chamber.\r\rMayor pro Tem Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian, to approve a revised letter to be sent from the City Attorney to the Calabasas Chamber to be copied to the Agoura-Conejo Chamber by a roll call vote.\r\rAYES: Mayor Wolfson, Mayor pro Tem Groveman, Councilmember Bozajian.\rNOES: Councilmember Maurer.\rRECUSED: Councilmember Washburn.\r\rADJOURN\r\r The City Council adjourned at 11:15 p.m. to their next regular meeting, which will be held on Wednesday, January 13, 2010 at 7:00 p.m.\r\r\r\r\r\r__________________________\rGwen Peirce, CMC, City Clerk\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00142\u0015\r\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00143\u0015\r12/09/09\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u00